/**
 * /horse-mats — "Zain Horse Mat — Heavy-Duty Horse Stable Flooring in Dubai"
 * conversion + SEO / AEO / GEO product landing page.
 *
 * Bespoke page (not the YAML-driven generic ProductPage), built to mirror the
 * sibling spokes src/pages/hammer-top.astro, src/pages/acoustic-strips.astro,
 * src/pages/screed-isolation.astro, src/pages/acoustic-underlay.astro and
 * src/pages/sports-track-underlay.astro — same class helpers,
 * progressive-enhancement scroll-reveal motion, hand-rolled breadcrumb and
 * combined JSON-LD @graph (prefix `hm-`).
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * This file serves /horse-mats. The content entry
 * src/content/products/horse-mats.yaml has been re-slugged from
 * `/horse-stable-mats/horse-mats` to `path: /horse-mats` and the matching branch
 * filtered out of getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same pattern
 * already used for acoustic-underlay, sports-track-underlay, screed-isolation,
 * acoustic-strips, hammer-top, zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo, zainactive-rolls
 * and curb-stone (and the /outdoor-pavers/dogbone + /hexagon re-slug). The YAML
 * entry stays as data (still a child of the `animal` hub); this file serves the
 * URL. Internal links that pointed at the old nested path were updated in
 * animal-agricultural-flooring.astro, shop.astro, hammer-top.astro,
 * blog/[slug].astro and src/content/posts/best-flooring-horse-stables-uae-climate.md.
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN / FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ─────────
 *  - PARENT HUB: the build request's breadcrumb JSON-LD names the parent
 *    "Horse Stable Mats" at /horse-stable-mats on host rukanalzain.com. That
 *    route does not exist in this project — the real parent hub is the animal
 *    category hub /animal-agricultural-flooring (horse-mats.yaml `hub: animal`,
 *    and that hub already lists this page under `children`). Both the visible
 *    breadcrumb and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below use the real path with the
 *    label "Animal & Agricultural Flooring" — the same substitution already made
 *    on the hammer-top and acoustic siblings. NOTE: public/images/
 *    horse-stable-mats-hub/ and the old `/horse-stable-mats/*` path prefix
 *    suggest a dedicated "Horse Stable Mats" sub-hub is planned. TODO: confirm
 *    the intended parent hub label / slug with the client; if the sub-hub ships,
 *    repoint crumb #2.
 *  - CANONICAL HOST: the request shows "rukanalzain.com/horse-mats"; the
 *    configured site is "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs — note the
 *    spelling: ruk*n*alzain, not ruk*an*alzain). Canonical + all schema URLs are
 *    built from the configured site via BaseLayout `canonical={PATH}` (same
 *    choice as the siblings). TODO: confirm the production domain / spelling.
 *  - DESIGN SYSTEM: the request describes a "Deep Navy/Slate #0f172a" theme with
 *    a #f59e0b accent and React/Lucide-React icons. This is a static Astro site
 *    (zero-JS) on the live charcoal / industrial-grey design system with a single
 *    amber action accent (tailwind.config.mjs, DESIGN-NOTES.md). The page follows
 *    that system; Lucide icons are inlined as raw SVG path data (no runtime) and
 *    the FAQ accordion uses native <details>/<summary>.
 *  - IMAGE PATHS: the request lists `src="/public/images/horse-mats/…"`. In Astro
 *    the `public/` directory IS the web root, so the served path is
 *    `/images/horse-mats/…` (used below).
 *  - TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS: horse-mats.yaml lists "Mat size" (mm),
 *    "Thickness" (mm) and "Surface texture options" as null "to collect", and
 *    DESIGN-NOTES.md / CLAUDE.md §6 say not to invent densities, thicknesses or
 *    tensile figures. Every spec row rendered below — including the density band
 *    (900–1100 kg/m³) and the 12/15/17/20 mm thickness list — is copy from the
 *    page-build request, NOT numeric data from
 *    "Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief V2.docx" or a manufacturer certificate.
 *    Treat the whole table as PROVISIONAL and confirm against real product data
 *    before go-live.
 *  - STRUCTURED DATA: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage) is emitted inline. The request supplied BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage. The FAQPage node is reproduced 1:1 from the on-page FAQ (the three
 *    questions from the request). The Product node keeps the request's `name`,
 *    `sku` (RZ-ZHM-01) and `brand`; the request's `offers` node is omitted — it
 *    carried no `price` (an incomplete Offer Google flags) and `areaServed` is
 *    not a valid Offer property. `areaServed` is kept on the Product instead,
 *    matching the hammer-top sibling. Organization JSON-LD is emitted sitewide
 *    by BaseLayout.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * public/images/horse-mats/ — intrinsic dimensions vary and are wired per-image
 * below to prevent layout shift. public/ images use a plain <img> (astro:assets
 * <Image /> only optimises src/assets imports; there is no
 * src/assets/images/horse-mats/ directory). Mapping request → file on disk:
 *   - zain-horse-mat-hero.jpg                     (1408×768, exact match)
 *   - zain-horse-mat-problem-solution.jpg         (1376×768, exact match)
 *   - zain-horse-mat-technical-specs.jpg          (1024×1024) — renamed on disk
